le up 8-13 despite a Dem-friendly midterm"], "rationale": "Alabama's deep Republican lean and Tuberville's dominant fundraising outweigh a midterm environment that favors Democrats; the latest polls, unanimous expert ratings, and prediction markets all point to a comfortable Republican win in this open-seat contest.", "watch": "Jones would need a late, oversized midterm wave plus substantial Republican crossover voting to close what polls put at a high-single-digit to low-double-digit gap.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Kay Ivey (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alabama's open governor's race pits Republican Senator Tommy Tuberville against Democrat Doug Jones, a former senator seeking a political comeback. The state's strong Republican lean frames the contest: its partisan baseline favors the GOP by about fifteen points, and every major race rating service calls the race solidly or safely Republican. Prediction markets give Jones roughly an eight percent chance of winning.\n\nTuberville holds a clear financial edge, having raised about three times as much as Jones and entering the fall with twice the cash on hand. Recent polls show him leading by eight to thirteen points, though polling in the state is sparse. Jones has campaigned actively on the Gulf Coast and in Mobile, and a midterm environment tilted toward Democrats offers his best opening. A Trump rally for Alabama Republicans underscores the nationalized framing that works in Tuberville's favor.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0254, "margin": -12.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0161, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0131, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0153, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-3